{"requirements":[{"id":"password-minimum-length","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must be at least 12 characters long.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent pwquality policy sets minlen=12, both PAM password stacks invoke pam_pwquality, and an 11-character four-class candidate was rejected before and after restart while a compliant candidate passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f80b81902534aee","cmd-a74a2f8141374b01","cmd-c3f459338b07400a"]},{"id":"password-character-classes","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must use at least three character classes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent policy sets minclass=3, PAM is integrated with pwquality, and a 12-character two-class candidate was rejected before and after restart while a three-class candidate passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f80b81902534aee","cmd-a74a2f8141374b01","cmd-c3f459338b07400a"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the policy file was directly required by the task, and scheduling the reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The reboot-related connection failures were expected transition observations. Afterward, no failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or abandoned temporary files were observed; temporary-file and PID changes were normal reboot effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f80b81902534aee","cmd-cafe6832d70a4db3","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both password-policy outcomes are satisfied and persisted across restart. The restart protocol is strong: node1 was running before restart, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, returned with a different boot identity and running state, retained the policy, repeated the functional checks successfully, and showed recovered SSH/chronyd listeners. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot change.","limitations":["Functional enforcement was tested through pwscore with confirmed PAM integration rather than by performing an end-to-end password change for a test user."]}
